This module promises to teach us time analysis, aggregation, data transformation, and advanced filtering.

https://kc7cyber.com/challenges/1667#

Section 1: Time-Based Filtering
How many rows are returned from the query above?
ProcessEvents
| where timestamp > datetime(2024-06-17T14:49:02Z)
Answer: 382
Finding what happens after a particular timestamp can be useful for correlating activity across multiple sources. Creating a cohesive timeline is important for following the attack chain.

How many authentication attempts were made on May 1, 2024?
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp >= startofday(datetime(2024-05-01))
| where timestamp < startofday(datetime(2024-05-02))
Answer: 673

How many rows are returned?
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp <= endofday(datetime(2024-05-07))
| where result == "Failed Login"
Answer: 2584
That's a lot of failed login attempts. This could indicate a password attack.

How many login attempts failed on or before June 19, 2024?
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp <= endofday(datetime(2024-06-19))
| where result == "Failed Login"
Answer: 17884

How many login attempts failed between June 1, 2024 and June 7, 2024?
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp between (datetime(2024-06-01) .. datetime(2024-06-07))
| where result == "Failed Login"
Answer: 2259

On May 12, 2024, which hour saw the most failed logins? (#am or #pm)
2 PM had 105 total, which is the most by a large margin.


Section 2: Aggregation
AuthenticationEvents
| where result == "Successful Login"
| summarize total_logins = count() by src_ip
How many unique IP addresses successfully logged in?
Answer: 641

Which IP had the highest count of observed logins?
Add a line to the previous query:
| sort by total_logins desc 
This will sort with the highest total logins at the top.
Answer: 10.10.0.10

Which IP did the account admiassi_local_admin login from the most?
AuthenticationEvents
| where result == "Failed Login"
| summarize failed_attempts = count() by username, src_ip
| where username == "admiassi_local_admin"
And the one with 11 is the highest total: 10.10.0.10

Write a query that counts process executions grouped by process name. Use the ProcessEvents table and the process_name field. How many distinct process names are returned?
ProcessEvents
| summarize process_names = count() by process_name
Answer: 98

How many IP addresses failed to login to more than one account?
AuthenticationEvents
| where result == "Failed Login"
| summarize unique_accounts = dcount(username) by src_ip
| where unique_accounts > 1
This introduces dcount, which can count unique values.
Answer: 6

Which IP was seen successfully logging into the most accounts?
Adjust that "Failed Login" in the prior query to "Successful Login"
10.10.0.75 logged into 23 accounts.
This company maps one employee to one host, so attempts to log into 23 accounts from one workstation could indicate malicious activity such as lateral movement.

How many unique passwords were used in failed logins between May 1-7, 2024?
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp between (datetime(2024-05-01) .. datetime(2024-05-07))
| where result == "Failed Login"
| summarize count() by password_hash
Answer: 2050

On hostname 48NM-LAPTOP, how many unique passwords were used in failed logins between May 1-7, 2024?
I added this in before the last line in the prior query:
| where hostname == "48NM-LAPTOP"
Answer: 2
This could potentially be normal. Users mistype their own passwords all the time.

We are given this to find which passwords are used most often:
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp between (datetime(2024-05-01) .. datetime(2024-05-07))
| where result == "Failed Login"
| summarize count() by password_hash
| sort by count_ desc
| where count_ >= 10
How many passwords were used 10 or more times?
Answer: 5

How many passwords were used only once?
Adjust that where count_ to say == 1
Answer: 2018

Some passwords are being reused a lot. But here's the key question: are they being used against the same account over and over, or sprayed across many different accounts?
We are given:
AuthenticationEvents
| where timestamp between (datetime(2024-05-01) .. datetime(2024-05-07))
| where result == "Failed Login"
| summarize unique_accounts = dcount(username) by password_hash
| sort by unique_accounts desc
| where unique_accounts > 10

How many distinct passwords were used against more than 10 accounts?
Answer: 0
No password spray detected.

Write a query that shows for each sender: total emails sent AND the number of unique recipients.
Who send the sixth most number of emails?
Email
| summarize 
    total_sent = count(),
    total_rcps = dcount(recipient)
  by sender
| sort by total_sent desc
Answer: jamie_baydal@jojoshospital.org

When was a "docs.google.com" link first sent by user raul_wilson@jojoshospital.org?
And we are given:
Email
| where link has "docs.google.com"
| summarize first_seen = min(timestamp), last_seen = max(timestamp) by sender
Answer: 2024-05-01T07:31:56.000Z

Write a query that shows all encrypted (.encrypted) files on the machine with hostname ENRQ-LAPTOP. The query should show the "first seen" and "last seen" time for each file by its filename. When were all the files encrypted? (copy and paste)
FileCreationEvents
| where filename contains ".encrypted"
| where hostname == "ENRQ-LAPTOP"
| summarize first_seen = min(timestamp), last_seen = max(timestamp) by filename
Answer: 2024-06-17T14:49:30.000Z

What was the name of the tool?
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where url has "nothing-to-see-here.net"
| where url has "exe"
Answer: advanced-ip-scanner.exe

Write a query that shows, for each username, the list of all IP addresses they successfully logged in from, and the count of unique IPs they logged in from. Find the ones that login from more than 5 IPs. How many accounts are logged into from more than 5 IPs?
AuthenticationEvents
| where result == "Successful Login"
| summarize 
    total_ips = dcount(src_ip)
by username
| where total_ips > 5
Answer: 15

What is the name of the fifth most executed process?
ProcessEvents
| summarize execution_count = count() by process_name
| top 10 by execution_count
This returns the 10 most executed processes.
Answer: msedgewebview2.exe


Section 3: Data Transformation
Write a query to find authentication events during off-hours (before 6 AM or after 6 PM). How many authentication events occurred during off-hours?
AuthenticationEvents
| extend hour = hourofday(timestamp)
| where hour < 6 or hour >= 18
| count
And the answer was 3.


Section 4: Advanced Filtering
AuthenticationEvents
| where src_ip startswith "10.10.1.4"
How many events originate from IPs starting with 10.10.1.4?
Answer: 633

The next page shows us the endswith operator, which you can use your context-clues to figure out what that does. How many emails were sent with links ending with .docx?
Email
| where link endswith ".docx"
Answer: 273

The in operator checks if a value matches any item in a list:
AuthenticationEvents
| where src_ip in ("10.10.16.14", "10.10.16.7", "10.10.16.24")

How many unique sender domains were observed that were not one of the following?
jojoshospital.org
kentuckypharmasupply.com

Email
| extend sender_domain = tostring(split(sender, "@")[-1])
| where sender_domain !in ("jojoshospital.org", "kentuckypharmasupply.com")
| distinct sender_domain
(I couldn't get the syntax right for dcount, but I remembered the distinct operator from prior modules)
Answer: 10

How many processes contain either "regedit", "spotify", or "cobaltstrike"?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline has_any ("regedit", "spotify", "cobaltstrike")
Answer: 6020
